<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Everything the app says, in the language it was written in.

    A translation is a file beside this one — `values-be/strings.xml`, `values-uk/strings.xml`
    — and nothing else changes. Which is the point: the words are here because a string typed
    into a composable is a word that can only ever be English.

    Two rules for anybody adding to this file:

    * **Name a string for what it says, not where it sits.** `settings_pace_detail` survives
      the panel being moved; `second_line_of_third_card` does not.
    * **Never build a sentence out of two of them.** Word order is not universal, and a
      translator handed half a sentence cannot fix the half they were not given. Use a format
      argument and let the whole sentence live in one entry.
-->
